{"p":{"slug":"afrodite-zegers","first":"Afrodite","last":"Zegers","cc":"GRE","iso":"gr","country":"Greece","g":1,"img":"https://platform.worldofsailors.com/storage/uploads/2026/08/1-afrodite-zegres-de-1787704734.webp","cm":161,"kg":58,"bio":"Afrodite Zegers-de Kleine – Autobiographical Summary\nI was born on 2 December 1991 in Athens, Greece, and moved to the Netherlands at the age of 19 due to family reasons. I hold both Greek and Dutch nationality, speak four languages, and live a life combining professional sport, law, music, and coaching.\nI am married to Rogier de Kleine, and we have two dogs, Senna and Charlie.\nI hold a Bachelor’s degree in Law from the University of Amsterdam (UvA) and a Master’s in Criminal Law with a specialization in Economic Criminal Law from the Open Universiteit. I currently work as a Change Manager in Financial Economic Crime – Transaction Monitoring at Rabobank in Utrecht.\nI am a certified Master Practitioner in Neuro-Linguistic Programming (NLP), applying communication and mindset coaching in both sport and professional settings.\nAlongside my legal and coaching work, I am an active classical pianist, having graduated from the Athens Conservatory at the age of 16, and I serve as Head Coach of the Optimist class at the DRCS Yacht Club in Switzerland.\nI have held the No. 1 world ranking (World Sailing) in the 470 class from 2017 to 2018, and have won national titles in both Greece and the Netherlands.\nSailing Career Highlights\nI began sailing at the age of 9, and have represented both the Netherlands and Greece in top-level international competitions, including two Olympic Games:","soc":{"facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/afrodite.kyranakou"},"rk":{"s":[749,1036.13,747,"2026-11-24",[16,"2021-04-13"]],"c":[37182,1,37109,"2026-11-24",[2635,"2020-08-25"]]},"st":{"ev":52,"win":3,"pod":10,"avg":19.9,"best":1},"cls":["470 (Women)","470 (Mixte)","Match Racing","SSL 47"],"recn":4},"res":{"s":[["2026-08-17","2026 470 World Championship",